# The .superpowers/ scratch tree: agent briefs, task reports, ledgers and review
# diffs. It is excluded one LEVEL at a time rather than with a plain
# `.superpowers/`, because a pattern that matches a DIRECTORY stops git's walk
# outright - so a `!` rule for a file inside it is never consulted, wherever it is
# written. Excluding the contents at each level and re-including the directories
# keeps the walk alive down to the two review gates below, which are shared
# tooling rather than scratch (committed in 86a3fcf). Everything else under here
# stays out of `git status`. Already-tracked files are unaffected either way:
# ignore rules only ever govern untracked paths.
.superpowers/*
!.superpowers/sdd
.superpowers/sdd/*
!.superpowers/sdd/redesign
.superpowers/sdd/redesign/*
!.superpowers/sdd/redesign/verify-g5.py
!.superpowers/sdd/redesign/check-added-copy.py
